2026-10-15T18:16:37.3503423Z === DST / quarter-grid (subprocess, HASTUB_TZ) ===
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3503432Z 
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3503550Z -- the stub honours HASTUB_TZ
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3503687Z   ok   dt_util carries the configured zone
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3503702Z 
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3503907Z -- solve anchor snaps to the quarter grid (coordinator path)
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3504072Z   ok   12:07:33 floors to 12:00:00 with tz and date intact
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3504204Z   ok   a boundary instant is its own anchor
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3504408Z   ok   optimize() receives the snapped anchor, not the raw 12:07 instant
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3504621Z   ok   every published plan timestamp lands on a :00/:15/:30/:45 boundary
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3504892Z   ok   step 0's price is the quarter in force at 12:07 — the 12:00 hour's
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3505100Z   ok   the wall-clock action lookup lands on step 0, no pre-horizon clamp
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3505267Z   ok   filed lead promises mature on quarter boundaries
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3505493Z   ok   an override expiring 12:05 still pins the [12:00, 12:15) step at 12:07
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3505659Z   ok   and frees every step starting at or past the expiry
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3506038Z   ok   the not-yet-expired override is kept, not dropped eagerly
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3506048Z 
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3506252Z -- window snap: day-anchored, across both DST transitions
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3506446Z   ok   15/30/60-minute snaps match the old keys exactly, fold included
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3506641Z   ok   the 25-hour autumn day meters 25 distinct 60-minute windows
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3506925Z   ok   120-minute windows advance the hour on the fold day (0,0,2,2,4,4,…)
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3507105Z   ok   and on the gap day, straight through the missing wall hour
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3507283Z   ok   a 12:10 and a 13:30 sample share one 120-minute window
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3507461Z   ok   elapsed inside a 120-minute window can exceed an hour
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3507656Z   ok   the window closes on the 2-hour boundary, not every wall hour
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3507855Z   ok   window_factors samples 12:00/14:00/16:00, not 13:00/15:00/17:00
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3507869Z 
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3508008Z -- planning grid on DST days (#243)
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3508175Z   ok   all six transition days align prices to real instants
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3508305Z   ok   the plain day stays a zero null
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3508504Z   ok   _forecast_arrays and _price_series agree on the spring grid
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3508662Z   ok   _Horizon.timestamps invents no spring phantom
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3508873Z   ok   one horizon clock: the coordinator's import IS the optimizer's
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3509051Z   ok   coordinator and optimizer stamp the same spring grid
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3509235Z   ok   and on a step that is not a whole number of minutes (spring)
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3509414Z   ok   coordinator and optimizer stamp the same autumn grid
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3509604Z   ok   and on a step that is not a whole number of minutes (autumn)
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3509782Z   ok   spring and autumn UTC gaps are 15 minutes, plain day too
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3509941Z   ok   spring plan books no energy on a phantom step
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3510095Z   ok   autumn plan max gap is one 15-minute step
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3510103Z 
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3510316Z -- window_factors across a transition INSIDE the horizon (#777)
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3510523Z   ok   the transition really is inside the autumn and spring horizons
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3510740Z   ok   autumn fold: every window bills under the hour the meter keys it at
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3510947Z   ok   spring gap: every window bills under the hour the meter keys it at
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3511165Z   ok   NULL CONTROL: the ordinary Saturday a week earlier never disagreed
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3511432Z   ok   and the comparison is not vacuous — both rates occur in every cell
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3511441Z 
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3511605Z -- age seams across the DST transitions (#1299)
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3511813Z   ok   a 2 h fold-night outage reads its true age, not the wall clock's
2026-10-15T18:16:37.3512010Z   ok   and crosses the 90-minute stale floor a 2 h outage must cross
